              "exam_name": "NEET 2015 · NCERT",
              "question": "<p>Two particles <span class=\"math-tex\">\\({A}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\">\\({B}\\)</span>, move with constant velocities <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\vec{v}_1\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\vec{v}_2\\)</span><sub> </sub>respectively. At the initial moment, their position vectors are <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\vec{r}_1\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\vec r_2\\)</span> respectively. The conditions for particles <span class=\"math-tex\">\\({A}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\">\\({B}\\)</span> for their collision will be:</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:500px;\"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\dfrac{\\vec{r}_1-\\vec{r}_2}{\\left|\\vec{r}_1-\\vec{r}_2\\right|}=\\dfrac{\\vec{v}_2-\\vec{v}_1}{\\left|\\vec{v}_2-\\vec{v}_1\\right|}\\)</span></td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\vec{r}_1 \\cdot \\vec{v}_1=\\vec{r}_2 \\cdot \\vec{v}_2\\)</span></td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\vec{r}_1 \\times \\vec{v}_1=\\vec{r}_2 \\times \\vec{v}_2\\)</span></td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\vec{r}_1-\\vec{r}_2=\\vec{v}_1-\\vec{v}_2\\)</span></td></tr></tbody></table>",
              "options": [
                "(1)",
